"program_narrative": "Program ERRPROC is a batch subprogram (standard error processing subroutine) that receives an error request LS-ERROR-REQUEST from its caller and returns with GOBACK. It opens the sequential file ERROR-LOG in extend (append) mode, captures a timestamp, and copies the caller's program ID, category, error code, severity, text and details into the ERR-MESSAGE record from copybook ERRHAND. It writes ERR-MESSAGE as one ERROR-LOG record, displays the same error details on the console between separator lines, and sets the caller's LS-RETURN-CODE to the requested severity. There is no loop. Error conditions handled: a non-'00' file status after OPEN or after WRITE is only displayed; processing is not stopped.",
